[{"id":"tools-order-simulate","itemId":"toolchain","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"Put in order what you do to see vote's waveform on your own computer.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">iverilog</code> turns the design and its testbench into one simulation, and <code class=\"nobreak\">vvp</code> runs it. The run writes the waveform file as it goes, so the viewer comes last: it can only draw what the run recorded.</p>","type":"order","steps":["Save `vote.sv` and `vote_tb.sv` in one folder.","Compile both files together with `iverilog`.","Run the result with `vvp`: the testbench prints its verdict and writes the waveform file.","Open the waveform file in a viewer and look at `a`, `b`, `c` and `y`."],"shuffled":[3,1,0,2]},{"id":"tools-fill-vcd","itemId":"toolchain","role":"core","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">vvp</code> has run this testbench. Type the name of the file your waveform viewer should open.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">$dumpfile</code> names the waveform file the run writes, here <code class=\"nobreak\">vote_tb.vcd</code>, and <code class=\"nobreak\">$dumpvars</code> records every signal of <code class=\"nobreak\">vote_tb</code> in it. A VCD file lists each change of each signal with its time, and the viewer draws those changes.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-00/vote/vote_tb.sv","firstLine":25,"totalLines":53,"before":["  initial begin"],"blankLine":{"left":"    $dumpfile(\"","right":"\");"},"after":["    $dumpvars(0, vote_tb);","    errors = 0;"],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"initial","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"begin","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]],"blankLine":{"left":[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"$dumpfile","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"\"","color":"var(--code-token-string-expression)","bold":false}],"right":[{"text":"\"","color":"var(--code-token-string-expression)","bold":false},{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]},"after":[[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"$dumpvars","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":", vote_tb);","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    errors ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":";","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]]},"accept":["vote_tb.vcd"],"caseSensitive":true,"blankLabel":"The file name"},{"id":"tools-order-debug","itemId":"toolchain","role":"stretch","promptHtml":"You changed <code class=\"nobreak\">vote.sv</code>, and the run printed <code>TEST FAILED: a=1 b=1 c=0 y=0, expected 1 at 20 ns</code>. Put your next steps in order.","explanationHtml":"<p>The time in a TEST FAILED line is when the check ran, at the end of the failing step, so the row to look at is the 10 ns before it. The waveform shows which signal is wrong there; you follow it back to the line that drives it and correct that line. Then you compile again before you run: <code class=\"nobreak\">vvp</code> alone would run the old simulation, built from the old <code class=\"nobreak\">vote.sv</code>.</p>","type":"order","steps":["Open the waveform file in the viewer.","Look at the step that ends at 20 ns, from 10 ns to 20 ns.","See that `y` is 0 there, although `a` and `b` are both 1.","Find the line of `vote.sv` that drives `y`, and correct it.","Compile with `iverilog`, then run with `vvp`, until the verdict is TEST PASSED."],"shuffled":[1,3,2,0,4]},{"id":"tools-fill-wait","itemId":"toolchain","role":"core","promptHtml":"This is the testbench for lesson 0.2's alarm, written like <code class=\"nobreak\">vote_tb.sv</code>. Each row should hold its inputs for 10 ns before <code class=\"nobreak\">siren</code> is checked. Type what makes the testbench wait.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">#10</code> waits 10 ns of simulated time; the first line of the file sets the unit to 1 ns. It is what turns each row into a 10 ns step on the waveform. Without it, all sixteen rows would happen at the same moment, time 0, and there would be no steps to see.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-00/alarm/alarm_tb.sv","firstLine":12,"totalLines":54,"before":["  // One row: armed, door_open and window_open, then the siren we expect.","  task automatic step(input logic va, input logic vd, input logic vw,","                      input logic want);","    armed       = va;","    door_open   = vd;","    window_open = vw;"],"blankLine":{"left":"    ","right":";"},"after":["    if (siren !== want) begin","      $display(\"TEST FAILED: %b%b%b gave siren=%b, expected %b at %0d ns\",","               armed, door_open, window_open, siren, want, $time);","      errors = errors + 1;","    end","  endtask"],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// One row: armed, door_open and window_open, then the siren we expect.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"task","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"automatic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"step","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","c